// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  NOT THE SOURCE OF TRUTH. DO NOT PASTE THIS INTO THE CONSOLE.
//
//  The rules currently PUBLISHED on chhota-e88e8 are broader than this file:
//  they cover users, menuItems, orders and counters, and they are stricter on
//  users than the block below. Publishing this file would DELETE the
//  menuItems / orders / counters rules and break Session 3 onward.
//
//  To edit rules, edit them in the Firebase console. This file is kept only as
//  a record of what the app relies on, and it needs to be replaced with a copy
//  of the live rules.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//  What the live users rules require (reported, worth re-reading in the console
//  before trusting): a create must be the caller's own uid and must contain
//  name, email, role and createdAt in the same write, with role either
//  'student' or 'vendor' and a non-empty name; an update may not change role.
//
//  src/services/userService.js satisfies all of this — it writes all four
//  fields in one setDoc and never updates a user document afterwards. Keep it
//  that way, or signup starts failing with permission-denied, which looks
//  identical to "rules were never published".
//
//  Session 3 note: read the live menuItems rules before writing menuService.js,
//  rather than assuming the shape.
//
// ─── historical: the users-only block from session 1, superseded ─────────────
//
